# The build happens inside the image, so nothing built or installed on the host
# should be copied in — a host node_modules would carry the host's platform
# binaries into a Linux container.
# Patterns are matched from the context root, so nested copies need `**/`.
# A stale tsbuildinfo copied in is not a harmless extra file: tsc --build reads
# it, concludes the output is current, and emits nothing at all.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets and runtime state reach the containers through compose, never a layer.
.env
.env.*
data

# Not needed to build or run anything.
.git
.github
docs
*.pdf
*.docx
*.md
!README.md
